## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical trade-offs in a globally distributed, sharded event store: shard key stability, cross-region replication, idempotence, and online resharding under SLA constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Consistent hashing for shard assignment and ring rebalancing
- Multi-region writes with quorum acknowledgments and leader/replica roles
- Idempotent writes using (tenant_id, event_id) and deduplication
- Conflict resolution using per-tenant clocks and commit timestamps
- Online resharding with versioned keyspaces and backfill strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
func writeEvent(tenantId, eventId, eventData) {
  // Determine shard using consistent hash
  shard = hashRing.getShard(tenantId)

  // Check for idempotency
  if (shard.exists(tenantId, eventId)) {
    return {status: "duplicate", sequence: shard.getSequence(tenantId, eventId)}
  }

  // Write with quorum
  sequence = shard.getNextSequence(tenantId)
  result = shard.writeWithQuorum(tenantId, eventId, eventData, sequence)

  return {status: "success", sequence: sequence}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical orchestration with event-sourcing and CQRS in a realistic CMS workflow; tests ability to model compensating actions and simple idempotent handlers, not just theory.

## Key Concepts

- Saga orchestration across services
- Compensation patterns (undo, release)
- Event-sourcing store of domain events
- Read models for article status
- Idempotent event handlers and outbox pattern

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch
class SagaOrchestrator {
  constructor(store) { this.store = store }
  startSaga(id) { this.store.appendEvent(id, 'DraftCreated', {}) }
  onEvent(e) {
    switch(e.type){
      case 'LicenseReserved':
        this.store.appendEvent(e.id, 'PaymentRequested', {})
        break;
      case 'PaymentProcessed':
        this.store.appendEvent(e.id, 'PublishRequested', {})
        break;
      case 'PaymentFailed':
      case 'LicenseReservationFailed':
        this.compensate(e.id)
        break;
    }
  }
  compensate(id){
    this.store.appendEvent(id, 'CancelDraft', {})
  }
}
```

